---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
// Keep this page true to the code: it describes what the site actually collects (newsletter:
// functions/api/subscribe.ts; quizzes and polls: functions/api/check/[slug].ts; ads: src/lib/ads.ts).
// Update it, and the date below, whenever one of those changes.
---
<Page
  title="Privacy"
  description="What The Learning Curve collects when you read, subscribe or answer a quiz, the cookies advertising may use, and how to ask about or delete your data."
  standfirst="We collect as little as we can: your email address if you subscribe, and nothing that identifies you otherwise."
>
  <p class="meta">Last updated 8 November 2026.</p>

  <h2>When you read</h2>
  <p>
    You can read every article without an account, and we don't set tracking cookies of our own. The site is hosted
    on Cloudflare, which handles each request and keeps routine logs (such as IP addresses) to run and protect the
    service. Fonts, search and images are served from our own site, and the share buttons are plain links, so no
    other company sees what you read here unless you click through to it.
  </p>
  <p>
    To count readers, we use Cloudflare Web Analytics. It records which pages are visited, the referring site, and
    the broad type of browser, device and country, without cookies, without fingerprinting and without following you
    across other sites. We see only totals, never individual visitors. Cloudflare explains it in
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" rel="noopener">its Web Analytics overview</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your browser stores two small things for your convenience only: whether you chose the light or dark theme, and
    your answers to any quiz or poll, so the results show again if you come back. They stay in your browser and you
    can clear them at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Quizzes and polls</h2>
  <p>
    When you answer a quiz or poll, we add your choices to that article's totals. To stop one browser being counted
    twice, we keep a one-way code made from your IP address, your browser and the article, mixed with a secret.
    We don't store your IP address or anything else that identifies you, and the totals can't be traced back to you.
  </p>

  <h2>The newsletter</h2>
  <p>
    If you subscribe, we send your email address to Beehiiv, the service that sends the newsletter, along with the
    page you signed up on. We use your address only to send the newsletter. Every email has a one-click unsubscribe link. Beehiiv's handling of your data is set out in
    <a href="https://www.beehiiv.com/privacy" rel="noopener">its privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    We never pass your address to anyone else, and we never sell or rent email addresses.
  </p>

  <h2 id="advertising">Advertising and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Some pages carry advertising (never reviews or comparisons). Ads booked directly with us are images served from
    our own site; clicking one takes you to the advertiser, whose own privacy policy then applies.
  </p>
  <p>
    Spaces with no direct booking may be filled by Google AdSense. When they are, Google and its partners use cookies
    and similar technologies to show ads, limit how often you see them and measure them, and may use information about
    your visits here and to other sites to show ads based on your interests. Visitors in the UK, the European Economic
    Area and Switzerland are asked for consent first and can change their choice at any time. You can learn
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from
    sites that use its services</a>, and turn personalised ads off in
    <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener">Google's ad settings</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Unsubscribe from the newsletter with the link at the foot of any issue.</li>
    <li>Clear this site's stored data in your browser's settings.</li>
    <li>Block or delete cookies in your browser, or use Google's ad settings to stop personalised ads.</li>
    <li>
      Ask what we hold about you, or ask us to correct or delete it, by emailing
      <a href="mailto:hello@thelearningcurve.net">hello@thelearningcurve.net</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>The Learning Curve is written for adults who build courses. It isn't aimed at children.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change what we collect, we'll update this page and the date at the top. How we're funded, including
    advertising and affiliate links, is on our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure page</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
